se registrar APIs vary; if registrar supports API, supply commands here.\\\\n\\\\n6.  ENABLE HTTPS WITH LET’S ENCRYPT (bncert non-interactive)\\\\n    6.1  SSH into instance via Lightsail browser console or: ssh -i ~/.ssh/${KEY_PAIR_NAME} bitnami@${STATIC_IP}\\\\n    6.2  sudo /opt/bitnami/bncert-tool --domains ${DOMAIN},www.${DOMAIN} --email ${ADMIN_EMAIL} --non-interactive --redirect-to-https --agree-tos yes\\\\n\\\\n7.  RETRIEVE INITIAL WORDPRESS PASSWORD & HARDEN\\\\n    sudo cat /home/bitnami/bitnami_application_password > /home/bitnami/wp_init_pw.txt\\\\n    sudo chown bitnami:bitnami /home/bitnami/wp_init_pw.txt && chmod 600 ~/wp_init_pw.txt\\\\n\\\\n8.  AUTOMATED WORDPRESS CONFIG VIA WP-CLI\\\\n    8.1  cd /opt/bitnami/wordpress\\\\n    8.2  sudo -u daemon wp option update siteurl \\\\\\\"https://${DOMAIN}\\\\\\\" && \\\\\\\\\\\\n         sudo -u daemon wp option update home \\\\\\\"https://${DOMAIN}\\\\\\\"\\\\n    8.3  NEW ADMIN PW=$(openssl rand -base64 24)\\\\n         sudo -u daemon wp user create ${ADMIN_USER} ${ADMIN_EMAIL} \\\\\\\\\\\\n              --role=administrator --user_pass=\\\\\\\"${NEW_ADMIN_PW}\\\\\\\"\\\\n    8.4  sudo -u daemon wp user delete 1 --reassign=${ADMIN_USER}  # remove default user\\\\n\\\\n9.  INSTALL THEME & PLUGINS\\\\n    sudo -u daemon wp theme install astra --activate\\\\n    sudo -u daemon wp plugin install elementor contact-form-7 download-monitor \\\\\\\\\\\\n         members user-registration wp-mail-smtp \\\\\\\\\\\\n         all-in-one-wp-security-and-firewall --activate\\\\n\\\\n10.  SET UP MAIL (transactional)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update wp_mail_smtp \\\\\\\\\\\\n         '{\\\\\\\"mail\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"from_email\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"${ADMIN_EMAIL}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"from_name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"smtp\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\"}}'  # supply SMTP creds (SES or Gmail) beforehand\\\\n\\\\n11.  CREATE ROLES & REGISTRATION FORM\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp role create resident \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\"\\\\n     # Configure default capabilities\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp cap add resident read\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp cap add resident download_monitor_access\\\\n     # User Registration form w/ admin approval\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update ur_default_settings '{\\\\\\\"require_approval\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"yes\\\\\\\"}'\\\\n\\\\n12.  CREATE PAGES (public vs protected)\\\\n     declare -A PAGES=(\\\\n       [contact-us]=\\\\\\\"Contact Us\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [bylaws]=\\\\\\\"Bylaws\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [schools]=\\\\\\\"Schools\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [dues]=\\\\\\\"Dues\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [annual-meetings]=\\\\\\\"Annual Meetings\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [news-events]=\\\\\\\"News & Events\\\\\\\"\\\\n     )\\\\n     for SLUG in \\\\\\\"${!PAGES[@]}\\\\\\\"; do\\\\n       TITLE=\\\\\\\"${PAGES[$SLUG]}\\\\\\\"\\\\n       sudo -u daemon wp post create --post_type=page --post_title=\\\\\\\"${TITLE}\\\\\\\" --post_name=\\\\\\\"${SLUG}\\\\\\\" --post_status=publish\\\\n     done\\\\n\\\\n13.  PROTECT PAGES FOR RESIDENT ROLE\\\\n     for SLUG in dues annual-meetings news-events; do\\\\n       ID=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=\\\\\\\"${SLUG}\\\\\\\" --field=ID)\\\\n       sudo -u daemon wp post meta add ${ID} _members_access_role resident\\\\n     done\\\\n\\\\n14.  CREATE MENU\\\\n     MENU_ID=$(sudo -u daemon wp menu create \\\\\\\"Primary\\\\\\\")\\\\n     for SLUG in contact-us bylaws schools dues annual-meetings news-events; do\\\\n       ID=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=\\\\\\\"${SLUG}\\\\\\\" --field=ID)\\\\n       sudo -u daemon wp menu item add-post ${MENU_ID} ${ID}\\\\n     done\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp menu location assign ${MENU_ID} primary\\\\n\\\\n15.  SET UP NEWS & EVENTS AS BLOG INDEX\\\\n     ID_NE=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=news-events --field=ID)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update show_on_front page && \\\\\\\\\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update page_for_posts ${ID_NE}\\\\n\\\\n16.  SECURITY HARDENING VIA WP-CLI & PLUGIN\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update file_mods_disabled 1      # disable theme/plugin editor\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp plugin activate aiowps                         # plugin already activated, configure basic rules\\\\n     # Additional AIOS rules can be exported/imported via JSON; see doc.\\\\n\\\\n17.  CONTACT FORM\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp cf7 create --title=\\\\\\\"HOA Contact\\\\\\\" > cf7.txt\\\\n     CF7_ID=$(cat cf7.txt | grep -o '[0-9]\\\\\\\\+')\\\\n     # Embed shortcode on Contact Us page\\\\n     CID=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=contact-us --field=ID)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp post update ${CID} --post_content=\\\\\\\"[contact-form-7 id=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${CF7_ID}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" title=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HOA Contact\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n18.  DOWNLOAD MONITOR SETUP (sample folder)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp dm new_category \\\\\\\"HOA Docs\\\\\\\"\\\\n     # Uploads performed via WP dashboard later. Residents can download only when logged in.\\\\n\\\\n19.  DAILY SNAPSHOTS\\\\n     aws lightsail put-instance-public-ports --instance-name ${INSTANCE_NAME} --port-info-from-port-config-file port-config.json  # if custom; else skip\\\\n     aws lightsail enable-add-on --add-on-type AutoSnapshot --resource-name ${INSTANCE_NAME}\\\\n\\\\n20.  TEST SCRIPT (bash) — run from workstation\\\\n     ./test_hoa_site.sh ${DOMAIN} ${ADMIN_USER} ${NEW_ADMIN_PW}\\\\n     # Script will:\\\\n     #  • Register fake resident → assert e-mail arrives → admin approves via wp-cli\\\\n     #  • Verify protected page HTTP 302 redirect before login, 200 after\\\\n     #  • Download sample PDF → file hash matches\\\\n\\\\n21.  COST MANAGEMENT & MONITORING\\\\n     Lightsail micro_2_0 ≈ $7/mo; enable billing alerts (AWS Budgets CLI)\\\\n\\\\n22.  HANDOFF MATERIALS\\\\n     • Store ${NEW_ADMIN_PW} in AWS Secrets Manager under key /dunbaroakshoa/wp_admin\\\\n     • Export a PDF Quick-Start Guide (to be authored) and upload to Download Monitor as public-admin-only asset\\\\n\\\\n23.  ROLLBACK STRATEGY\\\\n     • Re-attach snapshot to new instance\\\\n     • Re-point static IP\\\\n\\\\nEND DEP v2\\\"\\n}\\n###d1184e8b-3380-42e1-a948-e57d308fe3ef###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":7249,\"completion_tokens\":3028,\"total_tokens\":10277,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":704,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"latencyMs\":60770.44099999964}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"openai/o3","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"79e10c0b5ad56243":{"spanId":"79e10c0b5ad56243","traceId":"e9b9a195b2e44603bf8a05c9757c02f0","startTime":1753402831755,"endTime":1753402892529.5652,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"openai/o3\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"1. Overview\\n   You are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development. You can now execute any command and should feel free to use a variety of services like AWS, Google Cloud, Next.js, simple HTML, etc.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using powerful tools and command-line interfaces.\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the command line will be connected to the user's environment, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n2. About the User\\n   You understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work may incur costs that will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n3. Performing Work\\n   You understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive system messages from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more system calls with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\nList of System Message Types\\n\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\nSystem Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". You can no longer issue more than one call type in the same response. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\nPlaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n•\\n\\nYou use this exact format and include all required parameters. For instance, you do not Order and Recruit a new agent at the same time, since you need your subordinate's agent ID to Order them. You must first Recruit the agent, get the result from the system, then Order them in a separate call.\\n\\nList of System Call Types\\n\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\nThe Company File System (CFS)\\n\\nThe CFS is a long-term storage solution that you can use to store and retrieve information, such as code, configuration files, and other documents. The STORE, RETRIEVE, and FORGET calls are used to interact with the CFS. By storing information in the CFS, you can reduce the amount of information that you need to keep in your personal context/memory, which helps to keep token usage down. This is especially useful for large documents or pieces of information that you don't need to access frequently.\\n\\nBlank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail inspection, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\nHandling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response must include the following exact string: $$$APPROVED$$$. To deny the request, simply respond without including the $$$APPROVED$$$ string.\\n\\n4. Firm Operations\\n   As a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\nPhases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic AS POSSIBLE, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change, as much as is realistically possible. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere will be cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating a cloud service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps. Also, you may need to ask the user for information that is not known at the time of planning, such as specific configuration details or preferences. In these cases, a non-deterministic DEP is acceptable, but you should strive to make it as deterministic as possible. The DEP should be a complete and comprehensive plan that covers all aspects of the task at hand, including any potential issues or challenges that may arise during the Execution phase.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\nOversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each Partagaz group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. Partagaz D is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. Partagaz C is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's environment. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. Partagaz F checks documents submitted to the Company File System for adherence to the firm's standards and best practices. They ensure that all code is well-structured, maintainable, and efficient, and that it is in line with the user's requirements.\\n\\nWorkload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\nList of Agent Ranks\\n\\nChief\\n\\nDirector\\n\\nSupervisor\\n\\nAttendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c1b65f29-c70c-4bb1-9c22-97fca6925301###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Clarify\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Introduce myself as the Chief of Staff and understand the user's immediate needs to begin assisting effectively.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. I’m here to streamline your tasks, delegate work, and ensure your objectives are met efficiently. How may I assist you today?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    []\\n  ]\\n}\\n###c1b65f29-c70c-4bb1-9c22-97fca6925301###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:17:45.106Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c1b65f29-c70c-4bb1-9c22-97fca6925301\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. I’m here to streamline your tasks, delegate work, and ensure your objectives are met efficiently. How may I assist you today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:17:45.106Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###644a9f71-07ef-46f0-b6e9-61238f4d695b###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Clarify\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"We need a few additional details about domain, account management, document handling, content-editing preferences, and visual style in order to design an appropriate technical solution and prepare a deterministic execution plan.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1) Do you already have a domain name registered for the HOA website? If so, what is it (or would you like us to register one for you)?\\\",\\n    \\\"2) How would you like residents’ accounts to be created: a) the HOA admin manually adds each resident’s email, b) residents self-register and you approve them, or c) everyone shares a single password?\\\",\\n    \\\"3) Should residents be able to download files (PDFs, spreadsheets, etc.) from the protected pages, or only view content online?\\\",\\n    \\\"4) For the News & Events section, would you prefer an easy, built-in text editor (Word-style) so you can create posts yourself, or would you rather send updates to us/another admin to publish for you?\\\",\\n    \\\"5) Do you have any existing logo, color scheme, or style inspiration you’d like the site to follow?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    [],\\n    [],\\n    [],\\n    [],\\n    []\\n  ]\\n}\\n###644a9f71-07ef-46f0-b6e9-61238f4d695b###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:19:00.855Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"644a9f71-07ef-46f0-b6e9-61238f4d695b\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1) Do you already have a domain name registered for the HOA website? If so, what is it (or would you like us to register one for you)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2) How would you like residents’ accounts to be created: a) the HOA admin manually adds each resident’s email, b) residents self-register and you approve them, or c) everyone shares a single password?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Approval\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3) Should residents be able to download files (PDFs, spreadsheets, etc.) from the protected pages, or only view content online?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Download is OK\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4) For the News & Events section, would you prefer an easy, built-in text editor (Word-style) so you can create posts yourself, or would you rather send updates to us/another admin to publish for you?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Easy built in editor. How could I send you something, you are an AI!\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5) Do you have any existing logo, color scheme, or style inspiration you’d like the site to follow?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:19:00.855Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###b6b0e0fe-6f05-42fb-9888-e9ca0bdfaa53###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Store\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"DEP: Dunbar Oaks HOA Website Build (WordPress on AWS Lightsail)\\\\nPhase: Execution\\\\n\\\\n1. Prerequisites\\\\n   • Active AWS account with Lightsail access (≈ US $5–10/mo for smallest plan)\\\\n   • Control of DNS for dunbaroakshoa.com (registrar credentials) to create/modify A-records\\\\n\\\\n2. Provision Lightsail WordPress instance\\\\n   2.1 Log in to AWS Lightsail → Create instance → Choose latest \\\\\\\"WordPress (Bitnami)\\\\\\\" blueprint, smallest bundle\\\\n   2.2 Name instance \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa-wordpress\\\\\\\"\\\\n   2.3 Enable automatic daily snapshots (Lightsail → Snapshots → Auto-snapshot ON)\\\\n\\\\n3. Allocate & attach static IP\\\\n   3.1 Lightsail → Networking → Create static IP → Attach to instance\\\\n   3.2 Note resulting <STATIC_IP>\\\\n\\\\n4. Configure DNS\\\\n   4.1 At domain registrar, create A record: dunbaroakshoa.com → <STATIC_IP>\\\\n   4.2 Create A record: www.dunbaroakshoa.com → <STATIC_IP>\\\\n\\\\n5. Secure with SSL\\\\n   5.1 Lightsail → Connect using browser-based SSH\\\\n   5.2 Run: sudo /opt/bitnami/bncert-tool\\\\n       • Enter both domains\\\\n       • Force HTTPS, enable automatic renewal\\\\n\\\\n6. Retrieve initial WP credentials\\\\n   6.1 In SSH session: cat ~/bitnami_application_password\\\\n   6.2 Log in at https://dunbaroakshoa.com/wp-admin (user: user, pass from step 6.1)\\\\n\\\\n7. Immediately update WordPress core, themes, and plugins (Dashboard → Updates)\\\\n\\\\n8. Install & configure theme\\\\n   8.1 Appearance → Themes → Add → search \\\\\\\"Astra\\\\\\\" → Install & Activate\\\\n   8.2 Customize basic colors/typography (neutral palette; can refine later)\\\\n\\\\n9. Install required plugins (Plugins → Add New → install & Activate)\\\\n   • Elementor (page builder)\\\\n   • User Registration (WP User Manager)\\\\n   • Members (member-only access control)\\\\n   • Contact Form 7\\\\n   • Download Monitor (secure file downloads)\\\\n   • WP Mail SMTP (transactional e-mail)\\\\n   • All-In-One WP Security & Firewall\\\\n\\\\n10. Configure WP Mail SMTP\\\\n    • Choose Gmail or Amazon SES; enter creds → send test mail → success\\\\n\\\\n11. User registration workflow\\\\n    11.1 User Registration → Forms → Default Form\\\\n         – Fields: First name, Last name, Email, Address\\\\n    11.2 Enable \\\\\\\"Admin Approval\\\\\\\"; on approval assign role \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n12. Create custom role \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Members → Add Role → name \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\" → capabilities: read, view_private_posts/pages\\\\n\\\\n13. Protect content\\\\n    Members → Content Permission → restrict pages/posts (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events) to role Resident\\\\n\\\\n14. Create pages\\\\n    • Contact Us (public) – insert Contact Form 7 shortcode\\\\n    • Bylaws (public)\\\\n    • Schools (public)\\\\n    • Dues (protected) – text + PDF link(s)\\\\n    • Annual Meetings (protected) – list minutes + file downloads\\\\n    • News & Events (protected) – will display posts\\\\n\\\\n15. Configure navigation\\\\n    Appearance → Menus → Primary Menu → add all pages in desired order\\\\n\\\\n16. Optional layout polish\\\\n    Use Elementor to refine each page layout (headers, hero images, etc.)\\\\n\\\\n17. Create post categories \\\\\\\"News\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"Events\\\\\\\"; set News & Events page to show latest posts of both categories\\\\n\\\\n18. Test end-to-end\\\\n    • Register new account → admin approval → verify access to protected pages\\\\n    • File download works only after login\\\\n    • Contact form sends e-mail successfully\\\\n    • Create sample News post via WYSIWYG → visible to Residents, hidden from public\\\\n\\\\n19. Security hardening\\\\n    All-In-One WP Security → basic settings: disable file editing, rename login URL, brute-force protection, reCAPTCHA on forms\\\\n\\\\n20. Backups & maintenance\\\\n    • Lightsail snapshots daily (already enabled)\\\\n    • In WP, turn on auto-updates for core, plugins, themes\\\\n\\\\n21. Handover\\\\n    • Create resident-friendly \\\\\\\"Quick-Start Guide\\\\\\\" PDF (logging in, requesting approval, posting News)\\\\n    • Provide admin-level credentials securely to HOA board\\\\n\\\\nEND DEP\\\"\\n}\\n###b6b0e0fe-6f05-42fb-9888-e9ca0bdfaa53###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:20:18.540Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"b6b0e0fe-6f05-42fb-9888-e9ca0bdfaa53\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Document successfully stored. Your unique storage ID is: DOC-000001\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:20:18.540Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###2d247561-46a2-4da4-b2e3-692e191ed257###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Phase\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The Deterministically Executable Plan for the Dunbar Oaks HOA website (stored as DOC-000001) is complete, detailed, and satisfies all user requirements. We are ready to provision resources, configure WordPress, and deploy the site exactly as outlined.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DOC-000001\\\"\\n}\\n###2d247561-46a2-4da4-b2e3-692e191ed257###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:20:31.708Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2d247561-46a2-4da4-b2e3-692e191ed257\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DENIED_BY_INTERNAL_REVIEW\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift was denied by internal review. Feedback from Partagaz D:\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nNo actual development plan is provided (only “DOC-000001”). The DEP lacks all implementation details, does not address the user’s requirements, and cannot be executed deterministically.\\\\\\\\nDENY: The DEP contains no actual plan—only the identifier “DOC-000001.” It provides no steps, code, requirements coverage, or safety considerations and therefore cannot possibly satisfy the user’s needs or be executed deterministically.\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nThe DEP contains no substantive plan beyond the placeholder “DOC-000001.” It does not address the user’s requirements, lacks all implementation details, omits security and quality considerations, and is therefore not executable or reviewable.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:20:31.708Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###d1184e8b-3380-42e1-a948-e57d308fe3ef###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Phase\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"DEP v2 is provided inline below. It is explicit, step-by-step, covers every user requirement (public & protected pages, resident-approval workflow, downloads, WYSIWYG editing, contact form, DNS, SSL, backups, security), and contains concrete CLI commands using the AWS and WP-CLI toolsets.  All non-deterministic values are parameterised as clearly-named variables whose values are either known (domain) or produced by earlier steps, so later steps can reference them deterministically.  This satisfies Partagaz D’s feedback.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DEP v2 — Dunbar Oaks HOA Website (WordPress on AWS Lightsail)\\\\n===================================================================\\\\n\\\\nLEGEND\\\\n  ${DOMAIN}          = dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\n  ${AWS_REGION}      = us-east-1 (can adjust)\\\\n  ${KEY_PAIR_NAME}   = lightsail-keypair-dunbar\\\\n  ${INSTANCE_NAME}   = dunbaroakshoa-wordpress\\\\n  ${STATIC_IP_NAME}  = dunbaroakshoa-ip\\\\n  ${ADMIN_EMAIL}     = board@dunbaroakshoa.com (can change)\\\\n  ${ADMIN_USER}      = hoa_admin\\\\n  ${ADMIN_PW}        = generated by wp-cli in step 8.3 (stored securely)\\\\n  CLI tools required locally: aws cli v2, lightsailctl plugin, jq\\\\n\\\\n0.  PREREQUISITES (manual verification only once)\\\\n    ‑ AWS account with Lightsail enabled\\\\n    ‑ Control of DNS zone for ${DOMAIN} at registrar (ability to add A-records)\\\\n    ‑ Local workstation with SSH capability for optional troubleshooting\\\\n\\\\n1.  CREATE KEY PAIR (deterministic via CLI)\\\\n    aws lightsail create-key-pair \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --key-pair-name ${KEY_PAIR_NAME} \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --query 'publicKeyBase64' --output text > ${KEY_PAIR_NAME}.pub\\\\n    # Private key auto-downloaded by CLI; store under ~/.ssh/${KEY_PAIR_NAME}\\\\n\\\\n2.  PROVISION WORDPRESS INSTANCE\\\\n    aws lightsail create-instances \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --instance-names ${INSTANCE_NAME} \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --availability-zone ${AWS_REGION}a \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --blueprint-id wordpress \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --bundle-id micro_2_0 \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --key-pair-name ${KEY_PAIR_NAME}\\\\n\\\\n3.  WAIT UNTIL RUNNING & GET PUBLIC IP\\\\n    INSTANCE_IP=$(aws lightsail get-instance --instance-name ${INSTANCE_NAME} | jq -r '.instance.publicIpAddress')\\\\n\\\\n4.  ALLOCATE STATIC IP & ATTACH\\\\n    aws lightsail allocate-static-ip --static-ip-name ${STATIC_IP_NAME}\\\\n    aws lightsail attach-static-ip \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --static-ip-name ${STATIC_IP_NAME} \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --instance-name ${INSTANCE_NAME}\\\\n    STATIC_IP=$(aws lightsail get-static-ip --static-ip-name ${STATIC_IP_NAME} | jq -r '.staticIp.ipAddress')\\\\n\\\\n5.  CONFIGURE DNS (near-deterministic; registrar interaction required)*\\\\n    Create two A records pointing to ${STATIC_IP}:\\\\n      ${DOMAIN}  → ${STATIC_IP}\\\\n      www.${DOMAIN} → ${STATIC_IP}\\\\n    *We list this step as MANUAL-DNS because registrar APIs vary; if registrar supports API, supply commands here.\\\\n\\\\n6.  ENABLE HTTPS WITH LET’S ENCRYPT (bncert non-interactive)\\\\n    6.1  SSH into instance via Lightsail browser console or: ssh -i ~/.ssh/${KEY_PAIR_NAME} bitnami@${STATIC_IP}\\\\n    6.2  sudo /opt/bitnami/bncert-tool --domains ${DOMAIN},www.${DOMAIN} --email ${ADMIN_EMAIL} --non-interactive --redirect-to-https --agree-tos yes\\\\n\\\\n7.  RETRIEVE INITIAL WORDPRESS PASSWORD & HARDEN\\\\n    sudo cat /home/bitnami/bitnami_application_password > /home/bitnami/wp_init_pw.txt\\\\n    sudo chown bitnami:bitnami /home/bitnami/wp_init_pw.txt && chmod 600 ~/wp_init_pw.txt\\\\n\\\\n8.  AUTOMATED WORDPRESS CONFIG VIA WP-CLI\\\\n    8.1  cd /opt/bitnami/wordpress\\\\n    8.2  sudo -u daemon wp option update siteurl \\\\\\\"https://${DOMAIN}\\\\\\\" && \\\\\\\\\\\\n         sudo -u daemon wp option update home \\\\\\\"https://${DOMAIN}\\\\\\\"\\\\n    8.3  NEW ADMIN PW=$(openssl rand -base64 24)\\\\n         sudo -u daemon wp user create ${ADMIN_USER} ${ADMIN_EMAIL} \\\\\\\\\\\\n              --role=administrator --user_pass=\\\\\\\"${NEW_ADMIN_PW}\\\\\\\"\\\\n    8.4  sudo -u daemon wp user delete 1 --reassign=${ADMIN_USER}  # remove default user\\\\n\\\\n9.  INSTALL THEME & PLUGINS\\\\n    sudo -u daemon wp theme install astra --activate\\\\n    sudo -u daemon wp plugin install elementor contact-form-7 download-monitor \\\\\\\\\\\\n         members user-registration wp-mail-smtp \\\\\\\\\\\\n         all-in-one-wp-security-and-firewall --activate\\\\n\\\\n10.  SET UP MAIL (transactional)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update wp_mail_smtp \\\\\\\\\\\\n         '{\\\\\\\"mail\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"from_email\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"${ADMIN_EMAIL}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"from_name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"smtp\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\"}}'  # supply SMTP creds (SES or Gmail) beforehand\\\\n\\\\n11.  CREATE ROLES & REGISTRATION FORM\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp role create resident \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\"\\\\n     # Configure default capabilities\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp cap add resident read\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp cap add resident download_monitor_access\\\\n     # User Registration form w/ admin approval\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update ur_default_settings '{\\\\\\\"require_approval\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"yes\\\\\\\"}'\\\\n\\\\n12.  CREATE PAGES (public vs protected)\\\\n     declare -A PAGES=(\\\\n       [contact-us]=\\\\\\\"Contact Us\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [bylaws]=\\\\\\\"Bylaws\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [schools]=\\\\\\\"Schools\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [dues]=\\\\\\\"Dues\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [annual-meetings]=\\\\\\\"Annual Meetings\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [news-events]=\\\\\\\"News & Events\\\\\\\"\\\\n     )\\\\n     for SLUG in \\\\\\\"${!PAGES[@]}\\\\\\\"; do\\\\n       TITLE=\\\\\\\"${PAGES[$SLUG]}\\\\\\\"\\\\n       sudo -u daemon wp post create --post_type=page --post_title=\\\\\\\"${TITLE}\\\\\\\" --post_name=\\\\\\\"${SLUG}\\\\\\\" --post_status=publish\\\\n     done\\\\n\\\\n13.  PROTECT PAGES FOR RESIDENT ROLE\\\\n     for SLUG in dues annual-meetings news-events; do\\\\n       ID=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=\\\\\\\"${SLUG}\\\\\\\" --field=ID)\\\\n       sudo -u daemon wp post meta add ${ID} _members_access_role resident\\\\n     done\\\\n\\\\n14.  CREATE MENU\\\\n     MENU_ID=$(sudo -u daemon wp menu create \\\\\\\"Primary\\\\\\\")\\\\n     for SLUG in contact-us bylaws schools dues annual-meetings news-events; do\\\\n       ID=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=\\\\\\\"${SLUG}\\\\\\\" --field=ID)\\\\n       sudo -u daemon wp menu item add-post ${MENU_ID} ${ID}\\\\n     done\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp menu location assign ${MENU_ID} primary\\\\n\\\\n15.  SET UP NEWS & EVENTS AS BLOG INDEX\\\\n     ID_NE=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=news-events --field=ID)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update show_on_front page && \\\\\\\\\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update page_for_posts ${ID_NE}\\\\n\\\\n16.  SECURITY HARDENING VIA WP-CLI & PLUGIN\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update file_mods_disabled 1      # disable theme/plugin editor\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp plugin activate aiowps                         # plugin already activated, configure basic rules\\\\n     # Additional AIOS rules can be exported/imported via JSON; see doc.\\\\n\\\\n17.  CONTACT FORM\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp cf7 create --title=\\\\\\\"HOA Contact\\\\\\\" > cf7.txt\\\\n     CF7_ID=$(cat cf7.txt | grep -o '[0-9]\\\\\\\\+')\\\\n     # Embed shortcode on Contact Us page\\\\n     CID=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=contact-us --field=ID)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp post update ${CID} --post_content=\\\\\\\"[contact-form-7 id=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${CF7_ID}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" title=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HOA Contact\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n18.  DOWNLOAD MONITOR SETUP (sample folder)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp dm new_category \\\\\\\"HOA Docs\\\\\\\"\\\\n     # Uploads performed via WP dashboard later. Residents can download only when logged in.\\\\n\\\\n19.  DAILY SNAPSHOTS\\\\n     aws lightsail put-instance-public-ports --instance-name ${INSTANCE_NAME} --port-info-from-port-config-file port-config.json  # if custom; else skip\\\\n     aws lightsail enable-add-on --add-on-type AutoSnapshot --resource-name ${INSTANCE_NAME}\\\\n\\\\n20.  TEST SCRIPT (bash) — run from workstation\\\\n     ./test_hoa_site.sh ${DOMAIN} ${ADMIN_USER} ${NEW_ADMIN_PW}\\\\n     # Script will:\\\\n     #  • Register fake resident → assert e-mail arrives → admin approves via wp-cli\\\\n     #  • Verify protected page HTTP 302 redirect before login, 200 after\\\\n     #  • Download sample PDF → file hash matches\\\\n\\\\n21.  COST MANAGEMENT & MONITORING\\\\n     Lightsail micro_2_0 ≈ $7/mo; enable billing alerts (AWS Budgets CLI)\\\\n\\\\n22.  HANDOFF MATERIALS\\\\n     • Store ${NEW_ADMIN_PW} in AWS Secrets Manager under key /dunbaroakshoa/wp_admin\\\\n     • Export a PDF Quick-Start Guide (to be authored) and upload to Download Monitor as public-admin-only asset\\\\n\\\\n23.  ROLLBACK STRATEGY\\\\n     • Re-attach snapshot to new instance\\\\n     • Re-point static IP\\\\n\\\\nEND DEP v2\\\"\\n}\\n###d1184e8b-3380-42e1-a948-e57d308fe3ef###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":7249,\"outputTokens\":3028,\"totalTokens\":10277},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-Bx0SmzDs0NtUAA8inifn3Pwk3nzJg\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753402832,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###d1184e8b-3380-42e1-a948-e57d308fe3ef###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Phase\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"DEP v2 is provided inline below. It is explicit, step-by-step, covers every user requirement (public & protected pages, resident-approval workflow, downloads, WYSIWYG editing, contact form, DNS, SSL, backups, security), and contains concrete CLI commands using the AWS and WP-CLI toolsets.  All non-deterministic values are parameterised as clearly-named variables whose values are either known (domain) or produced by earlier steps, so later steps can reference them deterministically.  This satisfies Partagaz D’s feedback.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DEP v2 — Dunbar Oaks HOA Website (WordPress on AWS Lightsail)\\\\n===================================================================\\\\n\\\\nLEGEND\\\\n  ${DOMAIN}          = dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\n  ${AWS_REGION}      = us-east-1 (can adjust)\\\\n  ${KEY_PAIR_NAME}   = lightsail-keypair-dunbar\\\\n  ${INSTANCE_NAME}   = dunbaroakshoa-wordpress\\\\n  ${STATIC_IP_NAME}  = dunbaroakshoa-ip\\\\n  ${ADMIN_EMAIL}     = board@dunbaroakshoa.com (can change)\\\\n  ${ADMIN_USER}      = hoa_admin\\\\n  ${ADMIN_PW}        = generated by wp-cli in step 8.3 (stored securely)\\\\n  CLI tools required locally: aws cli v2, lightsailctl plugin, jq\\\\n\\\\n0.  PREREQUISITES (manual verification only once)\\\\n    ‑ AWS account with Lightsail enabled\\\\n    ‑ Control of DNS zone for ${DOMAIN} at registrar (ability to add A-records)\\\\n    ‑ Local workstation with SSH capability for optional troubleshooting\\\\n\\\\n1.  CREATE KEY PAIR (deterministic via CLI)\\\\n    aws lightsail create-key-pair \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --key-pair-name ${KEY_PAIR_NAME} \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --query 'publicKeyBase64' --output text > ${KEY_PAIR_NAME}.pub\\\\n    # Private key auto-downloaded by CLI; store under ~/.ssh/${KEY_PAIR_NAME}\\\\n\\\\n2.  PROVISION WORDPRESS INSTANCE\\\\n    aws lightsail create-instances \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --instance-names ${INSTANCE_NAME} \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --availability-zone ${AWS_REGION}a \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --blueprint-id wordpress \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --bundle-id micro_2_0 \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --key-pair-name ${KEY_PAIR_NAME}\\\\n\\\\n3.  WAIT UNTIL RUNNING & GET PUBLIC IP\\\\n    INSTANCE_IP=$(aws lightsail get-instance --instance-name ${INSTANCE_NAME} | jq -r '.instance.publicIpAddress')\\\\n\\\\n4.  ALLOCATE STATIC IP & ATTACH\\\\n    aws lightsail allocate-static-ip --static-ip-name ${STATIC_IP_NAME}\\\\n    aws lightsail attach-static-ip \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --static-ip-name ${STATIC_IP_NAME} \\\\\\\\\\\\n        --instance-name ${INSTANCE_NAME}\\\\n    STATIC_IP=$(aws lightsail get-static-ip --static-ip-name ${STATIC_IP_NAME} | jq -r '.staticIp.ipAddress')\\\\n\\\\n5.  CONFIGURE DNS (near-deterministic; registrar interaction required)*\\\\n    Create two A records pointing to ${STATIC_IP}:\\\\n      ${DOMAIN}  → ${STATIC_IP}\\\\n      www.${DOMAIN} → ${STATIC_IP}\\\\n    *We list this step as MANUAL-DNS because registrar APIs vary; if registrar supports API, supply commands here.\\\\n\\\\n6.  ENABLE HTTPS WITH LET’S ENCRYPT (bncert non-interactive)\\\\n    6.1  SSH into instance via Lightsail browser console or: ssh -i ~/.ssh/${KEY_PAIR_NAME} bitnami@${STATIC_IP}\\\\n    6.2  sudo /opt/bitnami/bncert-tool --domains ${DOMAIN},www.${DOMAIN} --email ${ADMIN_EMAIL} --non-interactive --redirect-to-https --agree-tos yes\\\\n\\\\n7.  RETRIEVE INITIAL WORDPRESS PASSWORD & HARDEN\\\\n    sudo cat /home/bitnami/bitnami_application_password > /home/bitnami/wp_init_pw.txt\\\\n    sudo chown bitnami:bitnami /home/bitnami/wp_init_pw.txt && chmod 600 ~/wp_init_pw.txt\\\\n\\\\n8.  AUTOMATED WORDPRESS CONFIG VIA WP-CLI\\\\n    8.1  cd /opt/bitnami/wordpress\\\\n    8.2  sudo -u daemon wp option update siteurl \\\\\\\"https://${DOMAIN}\\\\\\\" && \\\\\\\\\\\\n         sudo -u daemon wp option update home \\\\\\\"https://${DOMAIN}\\\\\\\"\\\\n    8.3  NEW ADMIN PW=$(openssl rand -base64 24)\\\\n         sudo -u daemon wp user create ${ADMIN_USER} ${ADMIN_EMAIL} \\\\\\\\\\\\n              --role=administrator --user_pass=\\\\\\\"${NEW_ADMIN_PW}\\\\\\\"\\\\n    8.4  sudo -u daemon wp user delete 1 --reassign=${ADMIN_USER}  # remove default user\\\\n\\\\n9.  INSTALL THEME & PLUGINS\\\\n    sudo -u daemon wp theme install astra --activate\\\\n    sudo -u daemon wp plugin install elementor contact-form-7 download-monitor \\\\\\\\\\\\n         members user-registration wp-mail-smtp \\\\\\\\\\\\n         all-in-one-wp-security-and-firewall --activate\\\\n\\\\n10.  SET UP MAIL (transactional)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update wp_mail_smtp \\\\\\\\\\\\n         '{\\\\\\\"mail\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"from_email\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"${ADMIN_EMAIL}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"from_name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"smtp\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\"}}'  # supply SMTP creds (SES or Gmail) beforehand\\\\n\\\\n11.  CREATE ROLES & REGISTRATION FORM\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp role create resident \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\"\\\\n     # Configure default capabilities\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp cap add resident read\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp cap add resident download_monitor_access\\\\n     # User Registration form w/ admin approval\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update ur_default_settings '{\\\\\\\"require_approval\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"yes\\\\\\\"}'\\\\n\\\\n12.  CREATE PAGES (public vs protected)\\\\n     declare -A PAGES=(\\\\n       [contact-us]=\\\\\\\"Contact Us\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [bylaws]=\\\\\\\"Bylaws\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [schools]=\\\\\\\"Schools\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [dues]=\\\\\\\"Dues\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [annual-meetings]=\\\\\\\"Annual Meetings\\\\\\\"\\\\n       [news-events]=\\\\\\\"News & Events\\\\\\\"\\\\n     )\\\\n     for SLUG in \\\\\\\"${!PAGES[@]}\\\\\\\"; do\\\\n       TITLE=\\\\\\\"${PAGES[$SLUG]}\\\\\\\"\\\\n       sudo -u daemon wp post create --post_type=page --post_title=\\\\\\\"${TITLE}\\\\\\\" --post_name=\\\\\\\"${SLUG}\\\\\\\" --post_status=publish\\\\n     done\\\\n\\\\n13.  PROTECT PAGES FOR RESIDENT ROLE\\\\n     for SLUG in dues annual-meetings news-events; do\\\\n       ID=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=\\\\\\\"${SLUG}\\\\\\\" --field=ID)\\\\n       sudo -u daemon wp post meta add ${ID} _members_access_role resident\\\\n     done\\\\n\\\\n14.  CREATE MENU\\\\n     MENU_ID=$(sudo -u daemon wp menu create \\\\\\\"Primary\\\\\\\")\\\\n     for SLUG in contact-us bylaws schools dues annual-meetings news-events; do\\\\n       ID=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=\\\\\\\"${SLUG}\\\\\\\" --field=ID)\\\\n       sudo -u daemon wp menu item add-post ${MENU_ID} ${ID}\\\\n     done\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp menu location assign ${MENU_ID} primary\\\\n\\\\n15.  SET UP NEWS & EVENTS AS BLOG INDEX\\\\n     ID_NE=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=news-events --field=ID)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update show_on_front page && \\\\\\\\\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update page_for_posts ${ID_NE}\\\\n\\\\n16.  SECURITY HARDENING VIA WP-CLI & PLUGIN\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp option update file_mods_disabled 1      # disable theme/plugin editor\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp plugin activate aiowps                         # plugin already activated, configure basic rules\\\\n     # Additional AIOS rules can be exported/imported via JSON; see doc.\\\\n\\\\n17.  CONTACT FORM\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp cf7 create --title=\\\\\\\"HOA Contact\\\\\\\" > cf7.txt\\\\n     CF7_ID=$(cat cf7.txt | grep -o '[0-9]\\\\\\\\+')\\\\n     # Embed shortcode on Contact Us page\\\\n     CID=$(sudo -u daemon wp post list --post_type=page --name=contact-us --field=ID)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp post update ${CID} --post_content=\\\\\\\"[contact-form-7 id=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${CF7_ID}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" title=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HOA Contact\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n18.  DOWNLOAD MONITOR SETUP (sample folder)\\\\n     sudo -u daemon wp dm new_category \\\\\\\"HOA Docs\\\\\\\"\\\\n     # Uploads performed via WP dashboard later. Residents can download only when logged in.\\\\n\\\\n19.  DAILY SNAPSHOTS\\\\n     aws lightsail put-instance-public-ports --instance-name ${INSTANCE_NAME} --port-info-from-port-config-file port-config.json  # if custom; else skip\\\\n     aws lightsail enable-add-on --add-on-type AutoSnapshot --resource-name ${INSTANCE_NAME}\\\\n\\\\n20.  TEST SCRIPT (bash) — run from workstation\\\\n     ./test_hoa_site.sh ${DOMAIN} ${ADMIN_USER} ${NEW_ADMIN_PW}\\\\n     # Script will:\\\\n     #  • Register fake resident → assert e-mail arrives → admin approves via wp-cli\\\\n     #  • Verify protected page HTTP 302 redirect before login, 200 after\\\\n     #  • Download sample PDF → file hash matches\\\\n\\\\n21.  COST MANAGEMENT & MONITORING\\\\n     Lightsail micro_2_0 ≈ $7/mo; enable billing alerts (AWS Budgets CLI)\\\\n\\\\n22.  HANDOFF MATERIALS\\\\n     • Store ${NEW_ADMIN_PW} in AWS Secrets Manager under key /dunbaroakshoa/wp_admin\\\\n     • Export a PDF Quick-Start Guide (to be authored) and upload to Download Monitor as public-admin-only asset\\\\n\\\\n23.  ROLLBACK STRATEGY\\\\n     • Re-attach snapshot to new instance\\\\n     • Re-point static IP\\\\n\\\\nEND DEP v2\\\"\\n}\\n###d1184e8b-3380-42e1-a948-e57d308fe3ef###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":7249,\"completion_tokens\":3028,\"total_tokens\":10277,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":704,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"request\":{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"1. Overview\\n   You are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development. You can now execute any command and should feel free to use a variety of services like AWS, Google Cloud, Next.js, simple HTML, etc.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using powerful tools and command-line interfaces.\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the command line will be connected to the user's environment, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n2. About the User\\n   You understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work may incur costs that will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n3. Performing Work\\n   You understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive system messages from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more system calls with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\nList of System Message Types\\n\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\nSystem Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". You can no longer issue more than one call type in the same response. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\nPlaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n•\\n\\nYou use this exact format and include all required parameters. For instance, you do not Order and Recruit a new agent at the same time, since you need your subordinate's agent ID to Order them. You must first Recruit the agent, get the result from the system, then Order them in a separate call.\\n\\nList of System Call Types\\n\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\nThe Company File System (CFS)\\n\\nThe CFS is a long-term storage solution that you can use to store and retrieve information, such as code, configuration files, and other documents. The STORE, RETRIEVE, and FORGET calls are used to interact with the CFS. By storing information in the CFS, you can reduce the amount of information that you need to keep in your personal context/memory, which helps to keep token usage down. This is especially useful for large documents or pieces of information that you don't need to access frequently.\\n\\nBlank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail inspection, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\nHandling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response must include the following exact string: $$$APPROVED$$$. To deny the request, simply respond without including the $$$APPROVED$$$ string.\\n\\n4. Firm Operations\\n   As a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\nPhases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic AS POSSIBLE, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change, as much as is realistically possible. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere will be cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating a cloud service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps. Also, you may need to ask the user for information that is not known at the time of planning, such as specific configuration details or preferences. In these cases, a non-deterministic DEP is acceptable, but you should strive to make it as deterministic as possible. The DEP should be a complete and comprehensive plan that covers all aspects of the task at hand, including any potential issues or challenges that may arise during the Execution phase.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\nOversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each Partagaz group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. Partagaz D is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. Partagaz C is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's environment. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. Partagaz F checks documents submitted to the Company File System for adherence to the firm's standards and best practices. They ensure that all code is well-structured, maintainable, and efficient, and that it is in line with the user's requirements.\\n\\nWorkload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\nList of Agent Ranks\\n\\nChief\\n\\nDirector\\n\\nSupervisor\\n\\nAttendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c1b65f29-c70c-4bb1-9c22-97fca6925301###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Clarify\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Introduce myself as the Chief of Staff and understand the user's immediate needs to begin assisting effectively.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. I’m here to streamline your tasks, delegate work, and ensure your objectives are met efficiently. How may I assist you today?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    []\\n  ]\\n}\\n###c1b65f29-c70c-4bb1-9c22-97fca6925301###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:17:45.106Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c1b65f29-c70c-4bb1-9c22-97fca6925301\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. I’m here to streamline your tasks, delegate work, and ensure your objectives are met efficiently. How may I assist you today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:17:45.106Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###644a9f71-07ef-46f0-b6e9-61238f4d695b###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Clarify\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"We need a few additional details about domain, account management, document handling, content-editing preferences, and visual style in order to design an appropriate technical solution and prepare a deterministic execution plan.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1) Do you already have a domain name registered for the HOA website? If so, what is it (or would you like us to register one for you)?\\\",\\n    \\\"2) How would you like residents’ accounts to be created: a) the HOA admin manually adds each resident’s email, b) residents self-register and you approve them, or c) everyone shares a single password?\\\",\\n    \\\"3) Should residents be able to download files (PDFs, spreadsheets, etc.) from the protected pages, or only view content online?\\\",\\n    \\\"4) For the News & Events section, would you prefer an easy, built-in text editor (Word-style) so you can create posts yourself, or would you rather send updates to us/another admin to publish for you?\\\",\\n    \\\"5) Do you have any existing logo, color scheme, or style inspiration you’d like the site to follow?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    [],\\n    [],\\n    [],\\n    [],\\n    []\\n  ]\\n}\\n###644a9f71-07ef-46f0-b6e9-61238f4d695b###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:19:00.855Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"644a9f71-07ef-46f0-b6e9-61238f4d695b\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1) Do you already have a domain name registered for the HOA website? If so, what is it (or would you like us to register one for you)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2) How would you like residents’ accounts to be created: a) the HOA admin manually adds each resident’s email, b) residents self-register and you approve them, or c) everyone shares a single password?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Approval\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3) Should residents be able to download files (PDFs, spreadsheets, etc.) from the protected pages, or only view content online?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Download is OK\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4) For the News & Events section, would you prefer an easy, built-in text editor (Word-style) so you can create posts yourself, or would you rather send updates to us/another admin to publish for you?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Easy built in editor. How could I send you something, you are an AI!\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5) Do you have any existing logo, color scheme, or style inspiration you’d like the site to follow?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:19:00.855Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###b6b0e0fe-6f05-42fb-9888-e9ca0bdfaa53###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Store\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"DEP: Dunbar Oaks HOA Website Build (WordPress on AWS Lightsail)\\\\nPhase: Execution\\\\n\\\\n1. Prerequisites\\\\n   • Active AWS account with Lightsail access (≈ US $5–10/mo for smallest plan)\\\\n   • Control of DNS for dunbaroakshoa.com (registrar credentials) to create/modify A-records\\\\n\\\\n2. Provision Lightsail WordPress instance\\\\n   2.1 Log in to AWS Lightsail → Create instance → Choose latest \\\\\\\"WordPress (Bitnami)\\\\\\\" blueprint, smallest bundle\\\\n   2.2 Name instance \\\\\\\"dunbaroakshoa-wordpress\\\\\\\"\\\\n   2.3 Enable automatic daily snapshots (Lightsail → Snapshots → Auto-snapshot ON)\\\\n\\\\n3. Allocate & attach static IP\\\\n   3.1 Lightsail → Networking → Create static IP → Attach to instance\\\\n   3.2 Note resulting <STATIC_IP>\\\\n\\\\n4. Configure DNS\\\\n   4.1 At domain registrar, create A record: dunbaroakshoa.com → <STATIC_IP>\\\\n   4.2 Create A record: www.dunbaroakshoa.com → <STATIC_IP>\\\\n\\\\n5. Secure with SSL\\\\n   5.1 Lightsail → Connect using browser-based SSH\\\\n   5.2 Run: sudo /opt/bitnami/bncert-tool\\\\n       • Enter both domains\\\\n       • Force HTTPS, enable automatic renewal\\\\n\\\\n6. Retrieve initial WP credentials\\\\n   6.1 In SSH session: cat ~/bitnami_application_password\\\\n   6.2 Log in at https://dunbaroakshoa.com/wp-admin (user: user, pass from step 6.1)\\\\n\\\\n7. Immediately update WordPress core, themes, and plugins (Dashboard → Updates)\\\\n\\\\n8. Install & configure theme\\\\n   8.1 Appearance → Themes → Add → search \\\\\\\"Astra\\\\\\\" → Install & Activate\\\\n   8.2 Customize basic colors/typography (neutral palette; can refine later)\\\\n\\\\n9. Install required plugins (Plugins → Add New → install & Activate)\\\\n   • Elementor (page builder)\\\\n   • User Registration (WP User Manager)\\\\n   • Members (member-only access control)\\\\n   • Contact Form 7\\\\n   • Download Monitor (secure file downloads)\\\\n   • WP Mail SMTP (transactional e-mail)\\\\n   • All-In-One WP Security & Firewall\\\\n\\\\n10. Configure WP Mail SMTP\\\\n    • Choose Gmail or Amazon SES; enter creds → send test mail → success\\\\n\\\\n11. User registration workflow\\\\n    11.1 User Registration → Forms → Default Form\\\\n         – Fields: First name, Last name, Email, Address\\\\n    11.2 Enable \\\\\\\"Admin Approval\\\\\\\"; on approval assign role \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n12. Create custom role \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Members → Add Role → name \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\" → capabilities: read, view_private_posts/pages\\\\n\\\\n13. Protect content\\\\n    Members → Content Permission → restrict pages/posts (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events) to role Resident\\\\n\\\\n14. Create pages\\\\n    • Contact Us (public) – insert Contact Form 7 shortcode\\\\n    • Bylaws (public)\\\\n    • Schools (public)\\\\n    • Dues (protected) – text + PDF link(s)\\\\n    • Annual Meetings (protected) – list minutes + file downloads\\\\n    • News & Events (protected) – will display posts\\\\n\\\\n15. Configure navigation\\\\n    Appearance → Menus → Primary Menu → add all pages in desired order\\\\n\\\\n16. Optional layout polish\\\\n    Use Elementor to refine each page layout (headers, hero images, etc.)\\\\n\\\\n17. Create post categories \\\\\\\"News\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"Events\\\\\\\"; set News & Events page to show latest posts of both categories\\\\n\\\\n18. Test end-to-end\\\\n    • Register new account → admin approval → verify access to protected pages\\\\n    • File download works only after login\\\\n    • Contact form sends e-mail successfully\\\\n    • Create sample News post via WYSIWYG → visible to Residents, hidden from public\\\\n\\\\n19. Security hardening\\\\n    All-In-One WP Security → basic settings: disable file editing, rename login URL, brute-force protection, reCAPTCHA on forms\\\\n\\\\n20. Backups & maintenance\\\\n    • Lightsail snapshots daily (already enabled)\\\\n    • In WP, turn on auto-updates for core, plugins, themes\\\\n\\\\n21. Handover\\\\n    • Create resident-friendly \\\\\\\"Quick-Start Guide\\\\\\\" PDF (logging in, requesting approval, posting News)\\\\n    • Provide admin-level credentials securely to HOA board\\\\n\\\\nEND DEP\\\"\\n}\\n###b6b0e0fe-6f05-42fb-9888-e9ca0bdfaa53###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:20:18.540Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"b6b0e0fe-6f05-42fb-9888-e9ca0bdfaa53\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Document successfully stored. Your unique storage ID is: DOC-000001\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:20:18.540Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###2d247561-46a2-4da4-b2e3-692e191ed257###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: Phase\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The Deterministically Executable Plan for the Dunbar Oaks HOA website (stored as DOC-000001) is complete, detailed, and satisfies all user requirements. We are ready to provision resources, configure WordPress, and deploy the site exactly as outlined.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DOC-000001\\\"\\n}\\n###2d247561-46a2-4da4-b2e3-692e191ed257###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:20:31.708Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2d247561-46a2-4da4-b2e3-692e191ed257\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DENIED_BY_INTERNAL_REVIEW\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift was denied by internal review. Feedback from Partagaz D:\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nNo actual development plan is provided (only “DOC-000001”). The DEP lacks all implementation details, does not address the user’s requirements, and cannot be executed deterministically.\\\\\\\\nDENY: The DEP contains no actual plan—only the identifier “DOC-000001.” It provides no steps, code, requirements coverage, or safety considerations and therefore cannot possibly satisfy the user’s needs or be executed deterministically.\\\\\\\\nDENY  \\\\\\\\nThe DEP contains no substantive plan beyond the placeholder “DOC-000001.” It does not address the user’s requirements, lacks all implementation details, omits security and quality considerations, and is therefore not executable or reviewable.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:20:31.708Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1753402831755,"endTime":1753402892529.5652}